{% comment %}
  Prints the product-page content that sits around the Amaze Price Builder
  calculator: the type eyebrow with its badge and dimension chip, the base
  rate line, the short description and spec list, and the "how this calculator
  works" panel from made-and-measured-demo-store.html.

  Rendered from a custom_liquid block in templates/product.json:

      {% render 'custom-product-info', product: product, part: 'head' %}

  Keeping the logic in a versioned snippet rather than typing Liquid into the
  block setting means it stays reviewable and every product page gets fixes at
  once. The block itself is one line.

  Nothing here touches the app's calculator form — the app owns that markup.

  Every field is optional. A product with no metafields set renders only what
  it can derive from product data, so this is safe to enable catalogue-wide
  before the metafields are filled in.

  Metafields read (namespace defaults to "custom"):
    calc_badge   single_line_text_field        "Area pricing"
    calc_dim     single_line_text_field        "W x H"
    calc_unit    single_line_text_field        "m2"
    calc_rate    single_line_text_field        "$85 / m2"  (overrides price)
    calc_short   single_line_text_field        one-line summary
    calc_specs   list.single_line_text_field   bullet list
    calc_logic   multi_line_text_field         the panel's paragraph(s)
    calc_accent  color                         per-product accent

  Accepts:
  - product:     {Object} the product (required). {% render %} isolates its
                 scope, so this must be passed explicitly rather than relied
                 on from the template.
  - namespace:   {String} metafield namespace. Default: 'custom'
  - rate_prefix: {String} label before the rate. Default: 'Base rate'
  - rate_suffix: {String} note after the rate. Default: 'final price built
                 from your inputs'. Pass '' to drop it.
  - part:        {String} 'head' (eyebrow + rate), 'body' (short, specs,
                 logic) or 'all'. The demo splits these around the form, so
                 use two blocks with 'head' above it and 'body' below.

  Usage:
  {% render 'custom-product-info', product: product, part: 'head' %}
  {% render 'custom-product-info', product: product, part: 'body' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign ns = namespace | default: 'custom'
  assign which = part | default: 'all'
  assign prefix = rate_prefix | default: 'Base rate'
  assign suffix = rate_suffix | default: 'final price built from your inputs'
  assign mf = product.metafields[ns]

  assign badge = mf.calc_badge.value
  assign dim = mf.calc_dim.value
  assign unit = mf.calc_unit.value
  assign rate = mf.calc_rate.value
  assign short = mf.calc_short.value
  assign specs = mf.calc_specs.value
  assign logic = mf.calc_logic.value
  assign accent = mf.calc_accent.value

  if accent == blank
    assign accent = '#004EBA'
  endif
  assign line = accent | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.1
  assign tint = accent | color_mix: '#FFFFFF', 8

  comment
    The rate line prefers an explicit metafield, then falls back to the
    product's own price so something sensible shows before anyone fills the
    field in.
  endcomment
  assign rate_value = rate
  if rate_value == blank and product.price > 0
    assign rate_value = product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Per-product accent handed to assets/custom-main-product.css, which uses it
  for the media crosshatch, the badge and the logic panel. Emitted only by the
  head part so two blocks on one page do not duplicate it. section.id is not
  reachable from inside a snippet, and a product page has exactly one product
  section, so .product is scope enough.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if which != 'body' -%}
  <style>
    .product {
      --pdp-hue: {{ accent }};
      --pdp-tint: {{ tint }};
      --pdp-line: {{ line }};
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="--pdp-info">
  {%- if which != 'body' -%}
  {%- if product.type != blank or badge != blank or dim != blank -%}
    <div class="--pdp-eyebrow">
      {%- if product.type != blank -%}
        <span>{{ product.type }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if badge != blank -%}
        <span class="--pdp-badge">{{ badge }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if dim != blank -%}
        <span class="--pdp-dim">{{ dim }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if rate_value != blank -%}
    <p class="--pdp-rate">
      {{ prefix }}
      <b>{{ rate_value }}</b>
      {%- if unit != blank %} / {{ unit }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if suffix != blank %} &middot; {{ suffix }}{% endif -%}
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if which != 'head' -%}
  {%- if short != blank -%}
    <p class="--pdp-short">{{ short }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if specs != blank and specs.size > 0 -%}
    <ul class="--pdp-specs" role="list">
      {%- for spec in specs -%}
        <li>
          {%- render 'custom-icons', name: 'check', size: 14, stroke: 2.4 -%}
          <span>{{ spec }}</span>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if logic != blank -%}
    <div class="--pdp-logic">
      <span class="--pdp-logic-kicker">How this calculator works</span>
      <div class="--pdp-logic-body">{{ logic | escape | newline_to_br }}</div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
